---
title: Cowboy caviar
yield: 8 cups
tags: [vegan, make-ahead, summer]
cuisine: american
source: Cowboy caviar by Margaux Laskey, NYT Cooking, https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1021230-cowboy-caviar
---

== Dressing ==

Whisk the @olive oil{1/4%cup}, @red wine vinegar{1/4%cup}, @garlic{3-4%cloves}(minced), @granulated sugar{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} in a #medium bowl{}.

== Salad ==

Add the @plum tomatoes{3}(cored, diced), @red onion{1/4%cup}(finely diced), @canned black beans{1}(15-oz can, rinsed), @black-eyed peas{1}(15-oz can, rinsed), @corn kernels{1 1/2%cup}(fresh from 2–4 cobs, or frozen and thawed), @bell pepper{1}(red, green or yellow; seeded, finely diced), @jalapeño{1}(seeded, finely diced) and @cilantro{1/3%cup}(leaves and tender stems, chopped).

Toss with the dressing and season with salt and pepper. Cover and chill ~{2%hours}.

Toss again and taste for seasoning. Scatter over the @?scallions{1}(chopped) and serve with @tortilla chips{}.
